  "source": "transformers.AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained('Xenova/c4ai-command-r-v01-tokenizer', use_fast=True).encode(input) - reference tokenizer.json is the one that ships in the upstream repo. transformers 5.14.1 / tokenizers 0.22.2.",
  "note": "CohereForAI/c4ai-command-r-v01 ships a byte-level BPE tokenizer with an NFC normalizer, a Sequence[Digits(individual_digits=true), ByteLevel] pre-tokenizer, and a TemplateProcessing post-processor that prepends <BOS_TOKEN> (id 5). Byte-level (GPT-2 family), no SentencePiece byte_fallback - the byte-to-char mapping covers non-vocab bytes. 255029-entry vocabulary with 37 added_tokens: 8 spec=true classical specials at ids 0-7 (<PAD>/<UNK>/<CLS>/<SEP>/<MASK_TOKEN>/<BOS_TOKEN>/<EOS_TOKEN>/<EOP_TOKEN>) plus 29 spec=false chat-template markers at ids 255000-255028 (<|START_OF_TURN_TOKEN|>, <|END_OF_TURN_TOKEN|>, <|USER_TOKEN|>, ...). Distinct shape from every previously-shipped fixture: first combination of NFC + Digits(individual_digits=true) + ByteLevel pre-tokenizer + TemplateProcessing(<BOS_TOKEN>). The upstream repo is gated; the tokenizer.json is fetched via the ungated Xenova tokenizer-only mirror (Xenova/c4ai-command-r-v01-tokenizer) whose blob is byte-identical to the upstream. Reference ids come from transformers.AutoTokenizer against that tokenizer.json. Pass criterion is byte-for-byte parity.",
